## Why This Is Asked
Interview to test token-based enrollment, per-tenant policy, and practical gateway validation with renewal and failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- Token-based enrollment (JWT)
- Short-lived client certificates (2h)
- Gateway tenant mapping and cert validation
- Renewal and revocation strategies
- Clock skew handling and audit logging

## Code Example
```javascript
function isCertValid(cert, now=new Date()) {
  const nb = new Date(cert.notBefore).getTime();
  const na = new Date(cert.notAfter).getTime();
  const skew = 5 * 60 * 1000; // 5 minutes
  if (now.getTime() < nb - skew) return false;
  if (now.getTime() > na + skew) return false;
  if (cert.subject?.CN !== cert.tenantId) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test renewal under clock skew and CA downtime?
- What logs/metrics ensure you can audit enrollment and revocation?

## Why This Is Asked

Explores KCA in latency- and connectivity-constrained edge deployments, with offline attestations and cross-region trust.

## Key Concepts

- Edge KCA workflows, offline attestation, short-lived certs
- Per-tenant store binding (SPIFFE IDs, scopes)
- Crypto agility (PQC fallback) and OTA signing
- Cross-region trust anchors and revocation/audit
- Testing for outages, handoffs, and tamper-evident logs

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: device attestation flow
function attestationFlow() {
  const boot = verifyHardwareRoot();
  const regional = attestToRegionalBootstrap();
  const csr = createCSR(storeId, scope);
  const cert = enrollToKCA(csr, ttl=300);
  if (!regional.connected) { useRecoveryToken(); }
  rotateIfNeeded();
  return cert;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you securely rotate keys during long outages?
- How do you verify audit logs across regions for a rollback scenario?
